Everything under this directory is a Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap.

  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License.
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

What is derived from OpenStreetMap

The questions name real places, brands, operators and wards, and those names
were read from OpenStreetMap, as was everything recorded about them:

  data/seeds/        the values, and what each one is in OpenStreetMap: its
                     tags, its element ids, how many features it matches
  data/questions/    the filled sentences, and the slot files they are made of
  data/originals/    the written sentences
  data/questions.jsonl
  data/README.md, data/provenance.yaml
                     which quote the same values as examples

data/templates/ holds sentences with their literal spans replaced by slots.
Those contain no value read from OpenStreetMap.

Where it was read from

Not from taginfo, and not from the live API. From one frozen extract:

  tokyo23-260831.osm.pbf
  md5 44a4ba2182379c147f20a27ad1b513ef, 87,399,745 bytes
  osm_base 2026-08-30T23:50:59Z

the twenty-three special wards of Tokyo cut from the OpenStreetMap planet file
of 2026-08-31, published as:

  https://huggingface.co/datasets/yuiseki/osm-tokyo23-src-2026-08

That extract was imported into a local Overpass API server, the
wiktorn/overpass-api image pinned in the source repository's
docker/compose.yml, and the scripts here asked that server. Doing it locally
against a pinned snapshot is what makes the resolution repeatable; an earlier
run asked a public Overpass instance holding a different snapshot and
disagreed, which is recorded in data/README.md. Both serve OpenStreetMap data
and both carry ODbL.

The planet file this all descends from:

  https://planet.openstreetmap.org/pbf/planet-260831.osm.pbf
  md5 c67437924cf55de40e8708c7192f354d

data/provenance.yaml records the rest: which values were checked, what was
checked about them, and what was deliberately left unchecked.

What is not derived from OpenStreetMap

The sentences are the author's own writing. A template, and a written question
before its values are put in, is prose a person composed, not a fact read out
of a database. The factual content of a filled question is from OpenStreetMap
and carries ODbL; the wording around it is the author's.

Answers

No answers are stored here. Answers computed from these questions against
OpenStreetMap are themselves derived from OpenStreetMap and carry ODbL.

